      "text": "To determine how many students did not receive an \"A\" in either math or history, we should first use the principle of inclusion and exclusion. The principle of inclusion and exclusion for two sets \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) is:\n\n\\[|A \\cup B| = |A| + |B| - |A \\cap B|\\]\n\nHere,\n- \\(|A|\\) represents the number of students that received an \"A\" in history,\n- \\(|B|\\) represents the number of students that received an \"A\" in math,\n- \\(|A \\cap B|\\) represents the number of students that received an \"A\" in both courses.\n\nGiven:\n- \\(|A| = 7\\)\n- \\(|B| = 13\\)\n- \\(|A \\cap B| = 4\\)\n- Total students = 30\n\nLet's calculate the number of students that received an \"A\" in at least one of the courses.\n\n\\[\n|A \\cup B| = 7 + 13 - 4\n\\]\n\nNext,\n- Subtract the number of students who received an \"A\" in both courses from the sum of the students who received an \"A\" in each course.\n\nFinally,\n- Subtract the number of students who received an \"A\" in at least one course from the total number of students.\n\nLet's compute this using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\ntotal_students = 30\nA = 7  # Students who received an A in history\nB = 13  # Students who received an A in math\nintersection = 4  # Students who received an A in both courses\n\n# Using the principle of inclusion and exclusion\neither_or = A + B - intersection\n\n# Either those who received A in only history or only math\neither_only = either_or - intersection\n\n# Students who did not receive an A in any course\nnone_of = total_students - either_or\nprint(none_of)\n```\n```output\n6\n```\nThe number of students who did not receive an \"A\" in either math or history is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
